2026-10-24T02:07:09.4135682Z Linux USB/IP device management (experimental preview)
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4135960Z 
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4136046Z Usage: rustusb [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4136204Z 
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4136270Z Commands:
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4136543Z   logs                Read sanitized stored logs or authorized agent audit projections
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4137028Z   agent               Run or query the nonroot shared application service using fixed profiles
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4137880Z   secure-server       Serve configured devices with mandatory mutual TLS and per-device authorization
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4138630Z   secure-discover     Read the stable-key device catalog over the configured mutually authenticated TLS endpoint
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4139308Z   secure-attach       Import the configured stable device key and own its encrypted VHCI relay until stopped
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4139929Z   native-pending      Inspect unresolved secure Native channels through the root helper (root only)
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4140541Z   native-reconcile    Verify a stopped Native channel and retire its record (root only; no USB writes)
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4141132Z   physical-pending    Inspect unresolved physical grants through the root helper (root only)
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4141749Z   physical-reconcile  Verify restored physical state and retire its grant record (root only; no USB writes)
2026-10-24T02:07:09.4142421Z   physical-server     Serve explicitly authorized whole USB devices through Linux USBFS (experimental, no TLS)
